Fix: RSD DTX services need the RSDCheckin handshake

pymobiledevice3's DtxServiceProvider._open_dtx_connection opens an RSD service
with a raw TCP connect (create_service_connection) and never performs the
RSDCheckin handshake. That is fine for RemoteXPC-native DTX services (e.g.
com.apple.instruments.dtservicehub), but lockdown-style shims advertised over
RSD with UsesRemoteXPC=False — such as
com.apple.accessibility.axAuditDaemon.remoteserver.shim.remote — require the
RSDCheckin exchange first. Without it, iOS 26 drops the connection on the first
DTX byte ("Connection was terminated abruptly").

This makes `pymobiledevice3 developer accessibility ...` work over a wireless
RemoteXPC tunnel (it previously only worked over USB).

The fix: for RemoteServiceDiscoveryService, use start_lockdown_service (which
performs RSDCheckin) instead of a raw create_service_connection.

--- a/pymobiledevice3/dtx_service_provider.py
+++ b/pymobiledevice3/dtx_service_provider.py
@@ _open_dtx_connection
         lockdown = self.lockdown
+        # Lockdown-style RSD services (UsesRemoteXPC=False, e.g. the
+        # *.shim.remote DTX daemons like axAuditDaemon) require the RSDCheckin
+        # handshake before they accept DTX framing; a raw TCP connect gets
+        # dropped on the first byte by iOS 26. start_lockdown_service performs
+        # RSDCheckin.
+        if isinstance(lockdown, RemoteServiceDiscoveryService):
+            svc = await lockdown.start_lockdown_service(service_name)
+            return DTXConnection(svc.reader, svc.writer)
         attr = await lockdown.get_service_connection_attributes(service_name, False)
         svc = await lockdown.create_service_connection(attr["Port"])
         await svc._ensure_started()
